    "6035beafb59dba80ee98b83b770b7ed8d9934ac05a449c8521fcec0154e72a24": {
      "normalizationVersion": 1,
      "sourceHash": "4a7b7e9be64e8ec492079f39acef48603152b4e72806110bf34adbb9bb2ce2a7",
      "contextFingerprint": "9af4eb33f1dd9b89812c327db136fa3427f2c0f07575095e4b21b91105f0177b",
      "sourceText": "* 函数指针保存函数地址，类型中包含函数的返回值和参数列表。\n* 函数名通常可以直接赋给签名兼容的函数指针。\n* 函数指针可以用于回调、运行时选择函数和函数表。\n* 静态成员函数可以使用普通函数指针。\n* 非静态成员函数需要成员函数指针，并且调用时必须提供对象。\n* 对象使用 `.*`，对象指针使用 `->*`。\n* `const` 是成员函数指针类型的一部分。\n* 可能为空的函数指针必须在调用前检查。\n* 现代 C++ 可以使用 `using` 简化类型，用无捕获 Lambda 创建函数指针。\n* 需要统一保存多种可调用对象时，可以使用 `std::function`。",
      "translatedText": "* A function pointer stores the address of a function, and its type includes the function's return value and parameter list\\.\n* The function name can usually be directly assigned to a function pointer with a compatible signature\\.\n* Function pointers can be used for callbacks, runtime function selection, and function tables\\.\n* Static member functions can use ordinary function pointers\\.\n* Non\\-static member functions require member function pointers, and the object must be provided when calling them\\.\n* Objects use `.*`; object pointers use `->*`\\.\n* `const` is part of the member function pointer type\\.\n* Function pointers that may be null must be checked before being called\\.\n* Modern C++ can use `using` to simplify types and create function pointers from captureless lambdas\\.\n* When multiple callable objects need to be stored uniformly, `std::function` can be used\\.",
      "provider": "deepseek",
      "model": "deepseek-flash",
      "usage": {
        "inputTokens": 265,
        "outputTokens": 174,
        "costUsd": 0.000289
      }
    },
